params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id: sprite } } (sprites\n- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArray, top row first, v \n- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and y), c, s (the turn's cosine and sine) }; null for an unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a collider\n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (distinct), pixels, bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1], rgba }; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shap\n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three \n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an a","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K4jjpmbJwCxa8wosjwLjru","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
