{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvX1wKQsQrEQqYwC1Uk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Em9iMSuvCKVXBJMDUpaW42","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, handoff copy)\n\nApplied by `python3 tools-gd/patch-engine.py my-3d2dge.js` (idempotent; the untouched copy is `.my-3d2dge.orig.js`).\n\n## E2: Humanoid gear (the only engine change)\n\n- **What:** new hand-held weapons `axe`, `bow`, `club`, `pan`, `scythe`, `fork` (with `tip()` lengths), an off-hand\n  `shield` (`offhand: 'shield'`, coloured by `colors.shield`), and two hats, `horned` (a helmet with curling horns,\n  `hat: { style: 'horned', horn }`) and `toque` (a cook's hat). Drawn in the HD path's depth-sorted list next to the\n  sword, so they sort with the arms in every view. Long hafts (scythe, fork) rest upright like the staff; the bow rests\n  forward and its string runs to the right hand while it is drawn.\n- **Why:** the heroes' and monsters' identities (the Berserker's axe and horns, the Shieldmaiden's shield, the Ranger's\n  bow, the Gnasher's club, the Fryar's pan, the Tithe's scythe, King Famish's carving fork, the Pot-Lobber's toque).\n- **Test:** `tests/sim.mjs`, \"the new gear is built in (no warnings)\": every weapon with a shield and the horned hat\n  updates and gives a tip with no \"not built in\" warning; screenshots of the class select and every floor.\n\n## Done in game code instead of the engine (planned as engine changes, not needed)\n\n- Multi-source flow field toward the nearest hero: `buildField()` in `game/src/21-world.js` (and `linkedField()` for\n  the bot, which also walks through transporter pairs).\n- Bouncing shots and shots that crack walls: the game's own projectiles (`stepShots()` in `23-monsters.js`).\n- A Create + Options guard: the session code ignores Options while `Pad8` is held; nothing binds Create.\n- PlayStation symbols by default with an Xbox option: the game's own `Button symbols` setting sets every player's\n  `input.glyphs`.\n- 10-foot HTML menus: a CSS `zoom` on the engine's `.esh` layer, sized from the window (`00-core.js`).\n- Per-player initials: the game's own letter wheel reads each qualifying player's input (`62-over.js`).\n- A voice bus: Babble's own gain node under the engine's master gain, with a `Voices` volume setting (`53-audio.js`).\nEOF\ncat > docs/DESIGNER.md <<'EOF'\n# Gauntletdown: building more of it\n\nContent is data in registries; the core never needs editing to add any of these.\n\n- **A floor:** `def('floors', id, { name, realm, no, rank, genRank, par, music, specials, amulets, rows })` in\n  `game/src/15-floors.js` (or lay it out with `tools-gd/floors.py`, which writes that file), then add its id to\n  `FLOOR_ORDER`. The legend is in `game/src/20-level.js` (`#` wall, `%` low accent wall, `X` cracked, `+` door, `T`/`Y`\n  trap walls with `^`/`v` plates, `?` fake wall, `~` lava, `O` transporter pairs in reading order, `!` stun rune,\n  `s` spikes, `|`/`-` force fields, `E` stairs, `2`-`9` skip stairs, `@` starts, items `k f b j z m u a $ * h l w B`,\n  monsters `g n o i y x t`, generators `G N L I F S`, `K` King, `=` table with `P` platters and `U` tureens).\n  `node tests/run.mjs floors` checks it is bordered, in the legend, its counts match and it can be finished.\n- **A monster:** `def('monsters', id, { name, hp, speed: [r1, r2, r3], dmg, points, ai, r, ... })` in `10-defs.js`, an\n  AI kind in `AI` (`23-monsters.js`) if it needs a new behaviour, and its rig in `monsterRig()` (`13-art.js`). Give it a\n  map character in `MON_CHAR` and a generator in `def('gens', ...)` / `GEN_CHAR`.\n- **An item:** `def('items', id, { name, pts, heal, food, shoot, treasure })`, its sprite in `buildArt()`, its effect in\n  `takeItem()` (`22-heroes.js`). Special potions and amulets are entries in `SPECIALS` and `AMULETS`.\n- **A narrator line:** a key in `LINES` (`05-text.js`), then `say(key, hero, priority)` where it happens. Keys starting\n  `tip_` play once per game.\n- **A song:** an entry in `SONGS` (`53-audio.js`), in the engine's step notation; name a track and set `on: false` to\n  make it a layer `layer(name, on)` brings in.\n- **Balance:** every number in `TUNE_SPEC` (`01-tune.js`) is a live slider in Dev Tools (pause menu); Reset puts them back.\nEOF\necho done","description":"Write engine-change notes and a designer guide"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":551907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":619},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28d8cdd1-64ac-4caf-98dc-e01333dcd3b0","uuid":"f4a33650-397d-47f0-9d95-d9ccc9f4fbc5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:56:11.458Z","request_id":"req_011CghvX1XkKsW8RELWKTaVw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Em9iMSuvCKVXBJMDUpaW42":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050247__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050247 && cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, handoff copy)\n\nApplied by `python3 tools-gd/patch-engine.py my-3d2dge.js` (idempotent; the untouched copy is `.my-3d2dge.orig.js`).\n\n## E2: Humanoid gear (the only engine change)\n\n- **What:** new hand-held weapons `axe`, `bow`, `club`, `pan`, `scythe`, `fork` (with `tip()` lengths), an off-hand\n  `shield` (`offhand: 'shield'`, coloured by `colors.shield`), and two hats, `horned` (a helmet with curling horns,\n  `hat: { style: 'horned', horn }`) and `toque` (a cook's hat). Drawn in the HD path's depth-sorted list next to the\n  sword, so they sort with the arms in every view. Long hafts (scythe, fork) rest upright like the staff; the bow rests\n  forward and its string runs to the right hand while it is drawn.\n- **Why:** the heroes' and monsters' identities (the Berserker's axe and horns, the Shieldmaiden's shield, the Ranger's\n  bow, the Gnasher's club, the Fryar's pan, the Tithe's scythe, King Famish's carving fork, the Pot-Lobber's toque).\n- **Test:** `tests/sim.mjs`, \"the new gear is built in (no warnings)\": every weapon with a shield and the horned hat\n  updates and gives a tip with no \"not built in\" warning; screenshots of the class select and every floor.\n\n## Done in game code instead of the engine (planned as engine changes, not needed)\n\n- Multi-source flow field toward the nearest hero: `buildField()` in `game/src/21-world.js` (and `linkedField()` for\n  the bot, which also walks through transporter pairs).\n- Bouncing shots and shots that crack walls: the game's own projectiles (`stepShots()` in `23-monsters.js`).\n- A Create + Options guard: the session code ignores Options while `Pad8` is held; nothing binds Create.\n- PlayStation symbols by default with an Xbox option: the game's own `Button symbols` setting sets every player's\n  `input.glyphs`.\n- 10-foot HTML menus: a CSS `zoom` on the engine's `.esh` layer, sized from the window (`00-core.js`).\n- Per-player initials: the game's own letter wheel reads each qualifying player's input (`62-over.js`).\n- A voice bus: Babble's own gain node under the engine's master gain, with a `Voices` volume setting (`53-audio.js`).\nEOF\ncat > docs/DESIGNER.md <<'EOF'\n# Gauntletdown: building more of it\n\nContent is data in registries; the core never needs editing to add any of these.\n\n- **A floor:** `def('floors', id, { name, realm, no, rank, genRank, par, music, specials, amulets, rows })` in\n  `game/src/15-floors.js` (or lay it out with `tools-gd/floors.py`, which writes that file), then add its id to\n  `FLOOR_ORDER`. The legend is in `game/src/20-level.js` (`#` wall, `%` low accent wall, `X` cracked, `+` door, `T`/`Y`\n  trap walls with `^`/`v` plates, `?` fake wall, `~` lava, `O` transporter pairs in reading order, `!` stun rune,\n  `s` spikes, `|`/`-` force fields, `E` stairs, `2`-`9` skip stairs, `@` starts, items `k f b j z m u a $ * h l w B`,\n  monsters `g n o i y x t`, generators `G N L I F S`, `K` King, `=` table with `P` platters and `U` tureens).\n  `node tests/run.mjs floors` checks it is bordered, in the legend, its counts match and it can be finished.\n- **A monster:** `def('monsters', id, { name, hp, speed: [r1, r2, r3], dmg, points, ai, r, ... })` in `10-defs.js`, an\n  AI kind in `AI` (`23-monsters.js`) if it needs a new behaviour, and its rig in `monsterRig()` (`13-art.js`). Give it a\n  map character in `MON_CHAR` and a generator in `def('gens', ...)` / `GEN_CHAR`.\n- **An item:** `def('items', id, { name, pts, heal, food, shoot, treasure })`, its sprite in `buildArt()`, its effect in\n  `takeItem()` (`22-heroes.js`). Special potions and amulets are entries in `SPECIALS` and `AMULETS`.\n- **A narrator line:** a key in `LINES` (`05-text.js`), then `say(key, hero, priority)` where it happens. Keys starting\n  `tip_` play once per game.\n- **A song:** an entry in `SONGS` (`53-audio.js`), in the engine's step notation; name a track and set `on: false` to\n  make it a layer `layer(name, on)` brings in.\n- **Balance:** every number in `TUNE_SPEC` (`01-tune.js`) is a live slider in Dev Tools (pause menu); Reset puts them back.\nEOF\necho done","description":"Write engine-change notes and a designer guide"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Em9iMSuvCKVXBJMDUpaW42":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050247__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050247"}}}
